        "name": "Juno 0.1.3",
        "notes": "# Cards that come filled in, tabs that stay, and replies in the right thread\n\n## What's new\n\n- Question cards come filled in: when a form asks something Juno can answer from what you told it, the card shows its suggestion and where it came from. Change any row or send it as is. Nothing is typed before your yes.\n- Write while a card waits: the card steps aside, Juno answers you, then asks again with a fresh card.\n- Replies land in their conversation: a reply to an email Juno read opens in that thread, with To and the subject filled in.\n- Juno checks before it answers: an answer that depends on your inbox, calendar, a page or a file reads it first. When it truly cannot look, it says so plainly.\n- Juno checks its own work in a document: after typing into a doc or a slide it looks at the result, and says so when it could not see it.\n- Your tabs stay: pages Juno opened for you are yours, never closed or reused by a later message. After a restart or an update they come back, each under the chat that opened it.\n- Pause a meeting recording: Pause on the notch stops the recording until you press Resume, and the transcript shows where the pause was. A recording stays small in the notch and opens when you point at it.\n- Copy or export a meeting: notes and transcript as Markdown, with each speaker and time. Card numbers and keys are always left out.\n- Continue in an earlier chat: when you bring up something an earlier chat was about, Juno offers to move your request there, one tap.\n- Sub-agents can read signed-in sites in their own background tabs, and a message you send while they work is read as your instruction.\n- Prices for your dates, in your currency: a hotel or travel price for other dates or in another currency is marked.\n- The app, not its website: when you have used a site's Mac app, like Discord, Juno goes to the app.\n- One card per file: a file changed several times in one answer shows as one card with its latest version and what changed.\n\n## Asks first\n\n- Sorting mail: labelling or archiving several selected emails shows one card listing every email and the labels it already has. Mail is sorted by reading each conversation, never by a search and Select all.\n- Changing who can see a file: \"Anyone with the link\", making something public or sharing it shows one card saying what will be seen by whom. Copying a link does not.\n- Agents use what they know and what you allowed: an agent no longer asks for a detail it already has, uses its permissions when you message it in its own chat, and never submits a form with a required question blank or guessed.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- Words on a page are not a button: clicking a slide's text or a text box that says \"checkout\", \"submit\" or \"delete\" no longer raises a Buy, Submit or Delete card. Typing into a field never does either. The real buttons still ask.\n- A chat shows the file that answers as its card; scripts and pictures made only to do the work go to a hidden .work folder.\n- A cookie notice over a button is cleared with the choice that shares the least, and Juno says which. Your yes is never spent on a press that cannot land.\n- Downloads work in your own tabs: the file saves to your Downloads folder and shows in the browser's list.\n- Editing a slide's text: Juno can click into a text that is a single letter, no longer asks for your mouse for a page open in its own browser, and can ask you a question while it works in a deck.\n- A chat's tab opens even when it is in another window after a restart: that window is brought forward.\n- The right Google account: Juno tries every account signed in before saying one is not, so Calendar opens as the account you named.\n- No more stuck \"Reading\": a tab that is not loaded, or not answering, no longer holds a task. Juno loads it, or opens the page in a fresh tab and says so.\n- An agent or routine added or changed outside Juno does not run until you confirm it.\n\nThe full notes are in What's new after the update.",
